{"repositoryId":870615857,"availability":"available","full":"0xvasanth/dataferry","name":"dataferry","description":"0xferry: a declarative data migration engine in Rust. Mongo→Postgres and Postgres→Postgres with split, merge, nest and unnest, resumable after crashes and verified by checksums.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":0,"forks":2,"created":"2024-10-10T11:11:46Z","updated":"2026-10-18T11:06:07Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://0xvasanth.github.io/dataferry/","topics":[],"demo":"https://0xvasanth.github.io/dataferry/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T18:19:24.685Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T18:19:24.685Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T18:19:24.685Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T18:19:24.685Z","stars":0,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An open-source data migration engine written in Rust. A declarative config in a ferry/ directory describes how data moves, and how it is reshaped, between data stores: 1:1 copies, splits into several tables, unnesting arrays into child tables, and merges of several entities into one table.","v0.1 moves MongoDB → Postgres and Postgres → Postgres, as a single-process CLI. Each partition commits on its own, so a run that stops halfway resumes where it left off and writes nothing twice (decision 0001).","The user guide covers every config key, the expression language and how runs resume. Each crate's API is on docs.rs (dataferry)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/0xvasanth/dataferry/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e9047a3a621703d8304cb910250ce906d8c3400edcc1760eb920740b803dd02a","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T18:19:24.786Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T18:19:24.786Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An open-source data migration engine written in Rust. A declarative config in a ferry/ directory describes how data moves, and how it is reshaped, between data stor